# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# There is no username or password here, and there never will be. Every
# connection in this repo authenticates with Microsoft Entra:
#
#   locally   your `az login` session
#   in Azure  the container's managed identity
#
# Same setting for both. Nothing to rotate, nothing to leak.

# ─── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The fully qualified server name.
#
# Fabric SQL Database:
#   your database -> Settings -> Connection strings
#   looks like:  abcdefghijk-xxxxxxxxxx.database.fabric.microsoft.com
#
# Azure SQL:
#   looks like:  myserver.database.windows.net
SQL_SERVER=

# The database name.
#
# CAREFUL: for a Fabric SQL database this is NOT just the item name. Fabric
# appends the item GUID, so a database you named "deposits" is actually:
#
#   deposits-aef098c2-f1e6-4bdd-b132-e8430f86b32f
#
# Copy the full value from Settings -> Connection strings. Using the short name
# fails with "Cannot open database".
#
# For Azure SQL and SQL Server it is just the database name.
SQL_DATABASE=

# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the MCP server is listening. Change this to point the helper scripts at
# a deployed instance instead of your laptop.
# DAB_MCP_URL=http://localhost:5000/mcp

# Override if you have a different ODBC driver installed. Driver 18 is required;
# Driver 17 uses older TLS defaults that Fabric rejects.
# ODBC_DRIVER=ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server

# ─── Stage two: the demo app ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed once you move past the server itself. See docs/06.

# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://<your-resource>.cognitiveservices.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4.1-mini

# ─── Stage three: the data agent comparison ──────────────────────────────────
# Only needed if you want the side-by-side. Leave unset and the compare toggle
# simply does not appear. See docs/07.
#
# NOTE: a Fabric data agent cannot set session context, so with claim-driven
# row-level security enabled it returns zero rows. Run
# sql/04-disable-row-level-security.sql before trying the comparison.

# FABRIC_WORKSPACE_ID=
# FABRIC_DATA_AGENT_ID=
